<h2>The practical takeaway</h2>
<p>
  For a single occasional task, iLovePDF's rate limit rarely matters. It becomes the actual friction point during batch work — processing a folder of scanned documents, prepping several files for the same submission, running the same operation across a class set of assignments. A browser-based tool with no server-side cost per task removes that specific ceiling, without asking for an account or a subscription. Keep a server-based tool bookmarked specifically for OCR or Word/Excel conversion, since that's the genuine gap a browser can't close yet.
</p>

